      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 9,
      "text": "2.  The instant petition has been preferred for challenging the order dated 03.07.2024 passed by learned Session Judge, Jhansi in Criminal Revision No.71 of 2023 (Rehan Khan and Another Vs.\nState of U.P. and Another), through which criminal revision preferred on behalf of respondent nos.2 and 3 has been allowed and order dated 03.01.2023 passed by learned Additional Civil Judge (J.D.)/Judicial Magistrate, Court No.1, Jhansi has been set-aside.\n3.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 484,
      "end": 934,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "03.07.2024",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 560,
          "end": 570
        },
        {
          "text": "Criminal Revision No.71 of 2023 (Rehan Khan and Another Vs.\nState of U.P. and Another",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 614,
          "end": 699
        },
        {
          "text": "03.01.2023",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 813,
          "end": 823
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submitted that learned court concerned has rightly summoned the respondent nos.2 and 3 in pursuance to sections 498A, 323, 504, 506, 420, 417, 313 I.P.C. and 3/4 D.P. Act vide order dated 22.11.2022, being aggrieved with the same, respondent nos.2 and 3 Smt Faraha Naz Khan vs State Of Up And 2 Others on 31 January, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/144287409/\n1 preferred Criminal Revision No.71 of 2023 (Rehan Khan and Another Vs. State of U.P. and Another), wherein learned revisional court without considering the facts and circumstances of the case, illegally and arbitrarily accepted the criminal revision and set-aside the summoning order.\n4. Considering the arguments raised by learned counsel for the petitioner and by bare perusal of record, it is crystal clear that no prejudice has been caused to the petitioner from the order passed by learned revisional court and as such no interference is required in the revisional order.\n5.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
